WEBVTT

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:12.099
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, all. Anyone watch the football last night? Honestly, I could've had that on in the background and missed absolutely nothing.</v>

00:00:13.509 --> 00:00:20.160
<v Callum Reid>Never mind that, whose new car's in the car park? Very shiny. Brave parking it next to the puddle.</v>

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:25.149
<v Jamie Brennan>Not mine. Mine's the one where the dirt's doing structural work.</v>

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:28.609
<v Aisha Begum>Protective coating, that. Engineering decision.</v>

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:34.329
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, Thursday 06 August. Let's get going before this becomes a car valuation meeting.</v>

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:39.390
<v Fiona Doyle>Um, can you hear me properly? Teams has picked a different microphone again.</v>

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:45.270
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, you're fine. Bit hollow, but we can hear you.</v>

00:00:47.189 --> 00:00:55.590
<v Sarah Okafor>Cal, can you sort the permit to work and isolation for the spinner by Thursday? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:00:57.859 --> 00:01:01.359
<v Callum Reid>By Thursday as in today, yeah? Not next week's Thursday.</v>

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:05.590
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, today. And first, because production's held up on it.</v>

00:01:06.319 --> 00:01:12.620
<v Callum Reid>Right, I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the spinner. Today, first thing in my order.</v>

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:18.129
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, the permit and isolation together, not just the bit of paper.</v>

00:01:19.329 --> 00:01:21.780
<v Callum Reid>Yep, understood. Both. That's what I'm taking.</v>

00:01:24.019 --> 00:01:29.620
<v Aisha Begum>While we're on the urgent ones, I'll replace the seals on the feed pump this morning.</v>

00:01:30.099 --> 00:01:31.849
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Ash. Top priority please.</v>

00:01:33.959 --> 00:01:38.859
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, I'll treat that as top priority. Seals on the feed pump, this morning.</v>

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:46.400
<v Fiona Doyle>Okay, so those are the two urgent bits, not everything on the list painted red.</v>

00:01:47.069 --> 00:01:53.719
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. The spinner comes first for Cal; Ash has the seals as top priority. Different people, no clash there.</v>

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:02.409
<v Hannah Price>Oh, before filters get mixed up again, I already swapped the filter on the guard switch on two yesterday.</v>

00:02:04.069 --> 00:02:08.270
<v Jamie Brennan>The one on two? Yeah, I nearly read that as still open.</v>

00:02:09.539 --> 00:02:13.389
<v Hannah Price>No, finished yesterday. That's an update, not another one for today.</v>

00:02:15.849 --> 00:02:20.750
<v Grace Liu>Different filter from me, then. I'll swap the filter on the IM1 hydraulic unit.</v>

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:26.599
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Grace Liu. Got you down for the IM1 hydraulic unit filter.</v>

00:02:27.139 --> 00:02:29.939
<v Grace Liu>Yep, that's mine. Not the guard switch one.</v>

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:37.199
<v Callum Reid>And I tested the big board yesterday and it's all fine now. While we're clearing the old stuff out.</v>

00:02:39.199 --> 00:02:43.050
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, so that's finished, rather than something still hanging over us?</v>

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:45.840
<v Callum Reid>Finished, yeah. All fine now.</v>

00:02:47.569 --> 00:02:52.469
<v Sarah Okafor>stores Jamie, can you check the guarding on the new line tomorrow at 9:30?</v>

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:58.319
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, I'll check the guarding on the new line tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:04.409
<v Fiona Doyle>Tomorrow being Friday, just so nobody's looking at the wrong day on Teams.</v>

00:03:05.569 --> 00:03:08.370
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, Friday at 9:30. That's the guarding check.</v>

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:13.629
<v Jamie Brennan>Understood. Not this morning. I've got the distinction.</v>

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:20.409
<v Hannah Price>Yeah so, I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the air dryer today.</v>

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:25.610
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Pricey. The air dryer sign-off is yours today.</v>

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:29.370
<v Hannah Price>Yep, I'll do that today.</v>

00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:37.759
<v Grace Liu>And that's the sign-off you're talking about, rather than another filter job? Sorry, people were talking over each other my end.</v>

00:03:40.199 --> 00:03:44.050
<v Hannah Price>The lock-out tag-out sign-off, yeah. Filter was the finished one yesterday.</v>

00:03:44.729 --> 00:03:50.680
<v Fiona Doyle>On the blocked stuff, I can't get to the alarm box until production gives us a window.</v>

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:55.729
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Still blocked, then. We're not allocating an alarm box job today.</v>

00:03:57.419 --> 00:04:00.569
<v Fiona Doyle>Exactly. No window, so it stays where it is.</v>

00:04:01.669 --> 00:04:09.020
<v Callum Reid>Same sort of story on the pump in the pit. Still waiting on parts, nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:04:10.979 --> 00:04:16.230
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, can't fit parts that aren't here. Much as the schedule would like us to.</v>

00:04:18.629 --> 00:04:23.180
<v Callum Reid>Quite. That's just the blocker carried over, not work I'm taking on today.</v>

00:04:24.509 --> 00:04:32.910
<v Fiona Doyle>Separate from that, I saw the pressure on the pump in the pit dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own.</v>

00:04:34.639 --> 00:04:36.740
<v Sarah Okafor>It recovered without anyone doing anything?</v>

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:43.060
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah. Few minutes, then back. Just an observation, not adding a job.</v>

00:04:45.199 --> 00:04:52.899
<v Sarah Okafor>I saw the pressure on the turbine one dip for a few minutes as well. That came back on its own too.</v>

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:56.449
<v Aisha Begum>Mm. Two observations, then. Doesn't tell us they're related.</v>

00:04:57.949 --> 00:05:02.850
<v Sarah Okafor>No, exactly. Not drawing a conclusion or putting another task on anyone from that.</v>

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:08.209
<v Callum Reid>And I'll inspect the Boiler Feedwater Pump for leaks after lunch.</v>

00:05:09.819 --> 00:05:16.470
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Cal, whenever you get a chance after lunch. That's not one to push ahead of the urgent stuff.</v>

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:23.769
<v Callum Reid>Yep. I'll inspect it after lunch, whenever I get a chance. Not treating it as urgent.</v>

00:05:25.269 --> 00:05:31.569
<v Fiona Doyle>Sorry, just keeping them straight in my head — Boiler Feedwater Pump inspection, not the feed pump seals?</v>

00:05:33.329 --> 00:05:38.930
<v Callum Reid>That's it. I'm inspecting the Boiler Feedwater Pump for leaks. Not taking the seals off Ash.</v>

00:05:40.009 --> 00:05:45.259
<v Aisha Begum>Definitely not. I'll replace the seals on the feed pump this morning, still top priority.</v>

00:05:47.209 --> 00:05:51.410
<v Hannah Price>Has stores Jamie frozen, or is that a very convincing listening face?</v>

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:53.600
<v Jamie Brennan>Listening face. Rarely seen, apparently.</v>

00:05:54.129 --> 00:05:56.579
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, anything unclear in what we've agreed?</v>

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:04.279
<v Fiona Doyle>No, that's clear. The finished bits stay finished and the blocked bits haven't magically become available.</v>

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:07.410
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. We'll leave it there, then. Cheers, everyone.</v>
